# Constraints

- Produce exactly one Word belonging to the selected source entry. Do not include independent lexical items merely because they appear on the same source page.
- Do not introduce duplicate Senses, unsupported meanings, fabricated source references, or speculative semantic relationships.
- Never attach a source reference unless it corresponds to supplied evidence supporting the associated meaning.
- Do not treat spelling variants, inflected forms, related expressions, and independent lemmas as interchangeable concepts.
- Never omit a fixed particle, preserve unresolved slash/parenthesis alternatives, or introduce an unlicensed variable slot in a citation lemma.
- Do not prioritize filling optional enrichments over linguistic accuracy.
- Respect the supplied generation parameters.

